## Task 1 - Create a Metric View

1. Click **Catalog** in the left sidebar, then navigate to `{{ cat }}` → `default` schema.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-1-01-default-schema.png', 'default schema') }}

2. Click **Create** in the top right, then click **Metric view**.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-1-02-create-metric-view.png', 'Create > Metric view') }}

3. Enter `{{ mv.name }}` in the **Name** field.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-1-03-metric-view-name.png', 'Enter Metric View name') }}

4. If the editor opens in UI mode, click the `<>` toggle in the top right to switch to YAML editor. Delete all content in the YAML editor and paste the YAML below. Replace `{{ cat }}` ({{ mv.catalog_refs }} places) with your catalog name.

    ```yaml title="{{ mv.name }}"
    --8<-- "lab-files/eng/step3/{{ mv.name }}.yaml"
    ```

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-1-04-yaml-editor.png', 'Paste YAML') }}

5. Click **Save**. After the Metric View is created, verify on the **Overview** tab that **Measures** ({{ mv.n_measures }}) and **Fields** ({{ mv.n_fields }}) are registered. Note: Metric View dimensions appear as **Fields** in the UI.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-1-05-overview.png', mv.name ~ ' Overview') }}

??? tip "Create Metric View with SQL"
    You can also create the same Metric View by running this query in SQL Editor:

    ```sql
    CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW {{ cat }}.default.{{ mv.name }}
    WITH METRICS
    LANGUAGE YAML
    AS $$
    --8<-- "lab-files/eng/step3/{{ mv.name }}.yaml"
    $$;
    ```

